  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provision of life saving assistance to people affected by the intensification of the conflict in Cit&#xE9; Soleil</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this project is to provide life-saving assistance to people affected by the spike in violence in Cit&#xE9; Soleil. This UNICEF project provides 1) US$ 43,200 in cash transfers for education to 720 people, 2) screening for 7,500 people for severe acute malnutrition, 3) four mobile child protection teams, and 4) US$ 100,000 in conditional cash transfers for WASH supplies for 15,000 people among other activities. The project provides life-saving assistance to 112,816 people, including 33,240 women, 27,700 men, 50,000 children, and 11,080 persons with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
